IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp4-assignment`
IMPORT `cp4-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer (cp4-seat.l4): at least one case per question, with the facts a real person in
-- the seat would state. Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text of the Act, as written beside the
-- assertion; none is copied from the encoding's own output. The Pension Index series, earnings and amounts are
-- invented for the cases, because they come from sections outside this piece. A case that expects NOTHING is a
-- case the Act, as read here, does not decide.

§ `Cases -- the individual's questions, Part II from section 55.2(5.2) to section 66.1`


§§ `Dividing earnings with a former spouse or partner (section 55.2 from subsection 5.2)`

-- Added and divided equally: (1000 + 3000) / 2.
#ASSERT `What second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings are attributed to me on the division` 1000 3000 EQUALS 2000
-- Base earnings divided under the Act (500) and a provincial plan (700): the aggregate, 1200.
#ASSERT `What are my total unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year of division where a provincial plan also divided them` `the base tier` TRUE 500 700 EQUALS JUST 1200
#ASSERT `What are my total unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year of division where a provincial plan also divided them` `the first additional tier` TRUE 250 150 EQUALS JUST 400
#ASSERT `What are my total unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year of division where a provincial plan also divided them` `the second additional tier` TRUE 100 20 EQUALS JUST 120
-- Not divided under both: the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `What are my total unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year of division where a provincial plan also divided them` `the base tier` FALSE 500 700 EQUALS NOTHING
-- We lived together that month, one of us contributed to a provincial plan, and it does not divide in a similar manner.
#ASSERT `Is the division barred for a month because one of us contributed to a provincial pension plan` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the division barred for a month because one of us contributed to a provincial pension plan` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Our base earnings together, 7000, do not exceed twice the Year's Basic Exemption (3500).
#ASSERT `Is no division of my earnings to be made for this month` `the base tier` (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) 7000 3500 (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1962 3 10) FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is no division of my earnings to be made for this month` `the base tier` (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) 7001 3500 (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1962 3 10) FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is no division of my earnings to be made for this month` `the first additional tier` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) 7000 3500 (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1962 3 10) FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- The younger of us turned 18 in March 1980: that month is before 18.
#ASSERT `Is no division of my earnings to be made for this month` `the second additional tier` (YearMonthDay 1980 3 1) 0 0 (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1962 3 10) FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is no division of my earnings to be made for this month` `the second additional tier` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) 0 0 (YearMonthDay 1960 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1962 3 10) FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Division in May 2020: paid from June 2020.
#ASSERT `From which month is my adjusted benefit paid after the division` (YearMonthDay 2020 5 17) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1)
-- Not for the month of the division or before.
#ASSERT `Can a benefit that was not payable without the division be paid to me for this month` (YearMonthDay 2020 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 5 17) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Can a benefit that was not payable without the division be paid to me for this month` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 5 17) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I and my former spouse or partner be notified of the division` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§§ `Applying late because of incapacity (section 55.3)`

-- The later of the first month a division could have taken place (May 2010) and the month incapacity began (February 2012): February 2012.
#ASSERT `Can the Minister treat my division application as made earlier because I was incapable when I applied` (YearMonthDay 2012 6 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 5 20) (YearMonthDay 2012 2 7) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2012 2 1)
-- The Minister is not satisfied.
#ASSERT `Can the Minister treat my division application as made earlier because I was incapable when I applied` (YearMonthDay 2012 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2010 5 20) (YearMonthDay 2012 2 7) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Stopped being incapable on 10 March 2015 after 100 days; applied on 17 June 2015, the last day of the window.
#ASSERT `Can the Minister treat my division application as made earlier because I was incapable until shortly before I applied` (YearMonthDay 2015 7 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 3 10) 100 (YearMonthDay 2015 6 17) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 20) (YearMonthDay 2012 2 7) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2012 2 1)
-- One day too late.
#ASSERT `Can the Minister treat my division application as made earlier because I was incapable until shortly before I applied` (YearMonthDay 2015 7 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 3 10) 100 (YearMonthDay 2015 6 18) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 20) (YearMonthDay 2012 2 7) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Disability pension (section 56)`

-- January 1966 to December 1990: 300 months.
#ASSERT `How many months are in my contributory period for a disability pension` (YearMonthDay 1940 2 2) (YearMonthDay 1990 12 1) (YearMonthDay 1991 6 1) 0 0 EQUALS 300
-- June 1988 to March 2010 is 262 months, less 10 and 5.
#ASSERT `How many months are in my contributory period for a disability pension` (YearMonthDay 1970 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2010 4 1) 10 5 EQUALS 247
#ASSERT `What is the flat rate part of my disability pension` 1986 (LIST 100, 103, 106) EQUALS JUST 91.06
-- 233.38 x 103/100.
#ASSERT `What is the flat rate part of my disability pension` 1987 (LIST 100, 103, 106) EQUALS JUST 240.3814
-- Before 1986 the Act gives no amount.
#ASSERT `What is the flat rate part of my disability pension` 1985 (LIST 100, 103, 106) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 25% of 120000 / 100.
#ASSERT `What part of my retirement pension from my base earnings counts for my disability pension` 1998 120000 100 0 0 EQUALS JUST 300
-- Neither subsection (4) nor (4.1) reaches a contributor deemed disabled in 1996.
#ASSERT `What part of my retirement pension from my base earnings counts for my disability pension` 1996 120000 100 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 8.33% of 240000 / 480 = 8.33% of 500.
#ASSERT `What part of my disability pension comes from my first additional earnings` 400 240000 999999 EQUALS 41.65
-- The 480 highest months: 288000 / 480 = 600; 8.33% of 600.
#ASSERT `What part of my disability pension comes from my first additional earnings` 481 240000 288000 EQUALS 49.98
-- 33.33% of 48000 / 480 = 33.33% of 100.
#ASSERT `What part of my disability pension comes from my second additional earnings` 100 48000 999999 EQUALS 33.33
#ASSERT `What part of my disability pension comes from my second additional earnings` 481 48000 96000 EQUALS 66.66
-- Flat rate 247.3828 plus 75% of (300 + 41.65 + 33.33) = 247.3828 + 281.235.
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly disability pension` 1988 (LIST 100, 103, 106) 1998 120000 100 0 0 400 240000 999999 100 48000 999999 EQUALS JUST 528.6178
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly disability pension` 1985 (LIST 100, 103, 106) 1998 120000 100 0 0 400 240000 999999 100 48000 999999 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (300 x 100 + 200 x 100) / 200.
#ASSERT `What base portion of my retirement pension counts for my disability pension after a division reduced it` TRUE 300 200 0 100 100 EQUALS JUST 250
#ASSERT `What base portion of my retirement pension counts for my disability pension after a division reduced it` FALSE 300 200 0 100 100 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Death benefit (section 57)`

-- Died in 2010: the lesser of 6 x 225 = 1350 and 10% of 40000, within the $2,500 cap.
#ASSERT `How much death benefit is paid to the estate of the contributor who died` (YearMonthDay 2010 3 15) FALSE 0 FALSE 120 120 108000 1 1 40000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 1350
-- Died after 2024 with no pension received and no survivor's pension: $5,000.
#ASSERT `How much death benefit is paid to the estate of the contributor who died` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) FALSE 0 FALSE 120 120 108000 1 1 40000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 5000
-- The contributor had received a pension: $2,500.
#ASSERT `How much death benefit is paid to the estate of the contributor who died` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) FALSE 0 FALSE 120 120 108000 1 1 40000 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 2500

§§ `Survivor's pension (section 58)`

-- 91.06 x 103/100 x 106/103.
#ASSERT `What is the flat rate part of my survivor's pension` 1988 (LIST 100, 103, 106) EQUALS JUST 96.5236
#ASSERT `What is the flat rate part of my survivor's pension` 1985 (LIST 100, 103, 106) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The pension began in July 2012; from then on the base portion is multiplied by 110/100.
#ASSERT `What base portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month` 300 (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2012 7 20)) 110 2010 2012 100 110 EQUALS JUST 330
-- Before the first event: not multiplied.
#ASSERT `What base portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month` 300 (YearMonthDay 2012 6 1) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2012 7 20)) 110 2010 2012 100 110 EQUALS JUST 300
-- Contributor died in 1970: the index without the limit (150) is used, 165/150 = 1.1.
#ASSERT `What base portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month` 300 (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2012 7 20)) 165 1970 1990 120 150 EQUALS JUST 330
-- 8.33% of 1000 x 120/100 = 99.96, then x 110/100.
#ASSERT `What first additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month` TRUE 1000 120 100 (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2012 7 20)) 110 100 EQUALS JUST 109.956
-- No pension payable at death: 83.3 x 1.1.
#ASSERT `What first additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month` FALSE 1000 120 100 (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2012 7 20)) 110 100 EQUALS JUST 91.63
-- 33.33% of 1000 = 333.3, x 1.1.
#ASSERT `What second additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month` FALSE 1000 120 100 (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2012 7 20)) 110 100 EQUALS JUST 366.63
-- Born 1975, the contributor died in March 2012: 100 months under 45, so 100/120 of 362.5 is taken away.
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I get no retirement pension` (YearMonthDay 2018 12 1) (YearMonthDay 1975 6 20) FALSE 100 400 100 200 FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) EQUALS JUST (362.5 DIVIDED BY 6)
-- From 2019 no reduction.
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I get no retirement pension` (YearMonthDay 2019 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1975 6 20) FALSE 100 400 100 200 FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) EQUALS JUST 362.5
-- Born 2 February 1950, 65 from March 2015: 60% of 700.
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I get no retirement pension` (YearMonthDay 2015 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1950 2 2) FALSE 100 400 100 200 FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 3 15) EQUALS JUST 420
-- Born 1940, 65 by 2010, retirement pension from 2005: paragraph (c).
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I also get a retirement pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1940 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1) 100 FALSE 0 400 100 200 200 50 25 0 60000 60000 1 EQUALS JUST 310
-- Under 65 with a retirement pension from after 1997: paragraph (a).
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I also get a retirement pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1) 100 FALSE 0 400 100 200 200 50 25 0 60000 60000 1 EQUALS JUST 277.5
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I also get a retirement pension` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2010 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1960 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2005 6 1) 100 FALSE 0 400 100 200 200 50 25 0 60000 60000 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `From which month am I qualified to receive my survivor's pension` (YearMonthDay 2010 3 20) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2010 4 1)
-- The aggregate 832.5 less the survivor's pension 300.
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly disability pension where I also get a survivor's pension` (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1990 1 1) 100 150 400 100 200 300 80 320 60000 60000 1 300 800 EQUALS 532.5
-- The disability pension alone is 900: subsection (6.1) saves it, 900 - 300.
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly disability pension where I also get a survivor's pension` (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1990 1 1) 100 150 400 100 200 300 80 320 60000 60000 1 300 900 EQUALS 600
-- Both in 1997: subsection (6.2).
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly disability pension where I also get a survivor's pension` (YearMonthDay 1997 12 31) (YearMonthDay 1997 6 1) 100 150 400 100 200 300 80 320 60000 60000 1 300 900 EQUALS 637.5
#ASSERT `How much is my survivor's pension if the Minister pays me the full disability pension instead` TRUE TRUE TRUE 832.5 700 EQUALS JUST 132.5
#ASSERT `How much is my survivor's pension if the Minister pays me the full disability pension instead` FALSE TRUE TRUE 832.5 700 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Subsection (8): 120 + 340 + 92.5 + 93 = 645.5, less 500.
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I also get a disability pension under a provincial pension plan` (YearMonthDay 1998 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1990 1 1) FALSE 100 120 400 100 200 250 70 30 60000 60000 1 500 EQUALS JUST 145.5
-- Subsection (8.1): 120 + min(612.5, 1250) = 732.5, less 500.
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I also get a disability pension under a provincial pension plan` (YearMonthDay 1997 12 31) (YearMonthDay 1997 6 1) FALSE 100 120 400 100 200 250 70 30 60000 60000 1 500 EQUALS JUST 232.5
-- An agreement under section 80 provides otherwise.
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I also get a disability pension under a provincial pension plan` (YearMonthDay 1998 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1990 1 1) TRUE 100 120 400 100 200 250 70 30 60000 60000 1 500 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Disabled contributor's child's benefit and orphan's benefit (section 59)`

-- 1992: 113.14 x 102/100 + 35 = 150.4028; 1993: x 105/102.
#ASSERT `How much is the monthly benefit for a child of a disabled contributor, or for an orphan` FALSE 1993 (LIST 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 102, 105, 105) EQUALS JUST (150.4028 TIMES 105 DIVIDED BY 102)
-- A part-time student gets 50%.
#ASSERT `How much is the monthly benefit for a child of a disabled contributor, or for an orphan` TRUE 1993 (LIST 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 102, 105, 105) EQUALS JUST (0.5 TIMES 150.4028 TIMES 105 DIVIDED BY 102)
#ASSERT `How much is the monthly benefit for a child of a disabled contributor, or for an orphan` FALSE 1990 (LIST 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 102, 105, 105) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Post-retirement benefit and post-retirement disability benefit (sections 59.1 and 59.2)`

-- 12000 x 0.9 / 40000 x 0.00625 x 50000 x 0.9 / 12.
#ASSERT `What is the base portion of my monthly post-retirement benefit` (YearMonthDay 1950 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) 0.9 1.42 FALSE 12000 40000 12 9000 10000 40000 50000 EQUALS JUST 6.328125
-- C = 0.00208.
#ASSERT `What is the first additional portion of my monthly post-retirement benefit` (YearMonthDay 1960 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) 2024 0.9 1.42 FALSE 12000 40000 12 9000 10000 40000 50000 EQUALS JUST 2.106
-- C = 0.00833.
#ASSERT `What is the second additional portion of my monthly post-retirement benefit` (YearMonthDay 1960 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) 0.9 1.42 FALSE 12000 20000 12 9000 10000 40000 50000 EQUALS JUST 8.434125
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly post-retirement benefit in all` 6.328125 2.106 8.434125 EQUALS JUST 16.86825
-- 485.20 x 102/100.
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly post-retirement disability benefit` 2019 (LIST 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 102, 105) EQUALS JUST 494.904
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly post-retirement disability benefit` 2020 (LIST 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 102, 105) EQUALS JUST 509.46
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly post-retirement disability benefit` 2018 (LIST 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 100, 102, 105) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Applying for a benefit (section 60)`

#ASSERT `Is a benefit payable to me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is a benefit payable to me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `On what day is my application for a post-retirement benefit treated as made` 2020 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1)
-- Born 1950, 70 from June 2020.
#ASSERT `May the Minister waive my application for a retirement pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1950 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Not yet 70 (deemed from 1 January 2022).
#ASSERT `May the Minister waive my application for a retirement pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1951 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2021 12 31) TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `On what day is my application for a retirement pension treated as made if the Minister waives it` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1)
-- The estate applies within 12 months after the death.
#ASSERT `May the application for a benefit of a person who has died be approved for this month` `a retirement pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2021 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2021 3 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 1940 2 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 3 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- A disability pension applied for after 1997 is excluded.
#ASSERT `May the application for a benefit of a person who has died be approved for this month` `a disability pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2021 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2021 3 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 1940 2 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 3 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `May an application be made for a child's or orphan's benefit after the child or orphan has died` `an orphan's benefit` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2015 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2000 8 10) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2016 6 15) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `May the benefit applied for after a death be paid to me as payee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `On what day is an application made after a death treated as received` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2015 6 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2015 6 15)
#ASSERT `Is my application for a benefit made as the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Minister consider my application at once and tell me the decision in writing` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The month before May 2010 is April 2010, later than November 2009.
#ASSERT `In which month can the Minister treat an application made for me as made because I was incapable` (YearMonthDay 2005 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 5 20) (YearMonthDay 2009 11 3) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2010 4 1)
#ASSERT `In which month can the Minister treat my application as made because I was incapable until shortly before I applied` (YearMonthDay 2005 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2012 3 10) 100 (YearMonthDay 2012 6 17) (YearMonthDay 2011 2 14) (YearMonthDay 2010 12 5) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2011 1 1)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister treat the application for my child's benefit as made in the same earlier month as my disability application` `a disability pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2011 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2012 6 5) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2011 1 1)
#ASSERT `Can the Minister treat the application for my child's benefit as made in the same earlier month as my disability application` `a retirement pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2011 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2012 6 5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must I be at the place and time the Minister requires to apply in person or give information` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§§ `Interim benefit (section 61)`

#ASSERT `May the Minister approve an interim benefit for me` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `How much more am I paid once my benefit is approved than my interim benefit` 800 1000 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `How much of my interim benefit must be deducted or recovered once my benefit is approved` 1000 800 EQUALS 200

§§ `When payment is made (section 62)`

-- First payable for January 2021, approved in March 2021.
#ASSERT `From which month are my monthly payments made` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2021 3 18) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1)
-- January, February and March are paid in one sum.
#ASSERT `For how many months am I paid in one sum` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2021 3 18) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `From which day is my benefit deemed to have become payable` (YearMonthDay 2021 4 17) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1)

§§ `Remarriage and the survivor's pension (sections 63 and 63.1)`

-- (The day section 63.1 came into force is not in the text; 1 January 1987 is invented for the case.)
#ASSERT `Is no survivor's pension payable to me while I am remarried` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1985 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Remarried after section 63.1.
#ASSERT `Is no survivor's pension payable to me while I am remarried` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1990 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my first deceased spouse treated as the spouse named in my application for a survivor's pension after a later death` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1985 5 5) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `From which month is my survivor's pension discontinued because I remarried` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1985 5 17) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1985 6 1)
#ASSERT `What survivor's pension am I paid on application if my new spouse dies` TRUE TRUE 500 700 EQUALS JUST 700
#ASSERT `What survivor's pension am I paid on application if my new spouse dies` FALSE TRUE 500 700 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does my discontinued survivor's pension become payable again when my later marriage ends` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1986 6 1) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my basic monthly amount calculated as though my survivor's pension had never been discontinued` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Which one survivor's pension am I paid if more than one would be payable` (LIST 300, 500, 400) EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `Is my survivor's pension withheld because the contributor died within a year of our marriage` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2020 12 1) FALSE 100 50 EQUALS TRUE
-- 365 days of cohabitation in all: subsection (7.1).
#ASSERT `Is my survivor's pension withheld because the contributor died within a year of our marriage` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2020 12 1) FALSE 200 165 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `May I apply in writing for my survivor's pension to be commenced or reinstated` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- The eleventh month before June 1988 is July 1987.
#ASSERT `From which month is my survivor's pension payable once my application is approved` (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1988 6 15) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 1987 7 1)
#ASSERT `From what time is my basic monthly amount worked out under section 58` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1984 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1980 9 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 1984 3 1)

§§ `Protection of a benefit (section 65)`

#ASSERT `Is a dealing with my benefit void` `an assignment of a benefit` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- An assignment approved under section 65.1 is not void.
#ASSERT `Is a dealing with my benefit void` `an assignment of a benefit` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my benefit exempt from seizure and execution` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `How much may the Minister deduct from my benefit to repay a provincial or municipal authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE 400 1000 EQUALS JUST 400
#ASSERT `How much may the Minister deduct from my disability benefit to repay a disability income program` `a disability pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 300 1000 TRUE EQUALS JUST 300
-- Regulation 76.1: the amount must exceed $50.
#ASSERT `How much may the Minister deduct from my disability benefit to repay a disability income program` `a disability pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 1000 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Assigning part of my retirement pension to my spouse or partner (section 65.1)`

#ASSERT `Does our agreement stop the Minister approving an assignment` (YearMonthDay 1990 1 1) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1995 1 1) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Not binding: they do not bind the Minister.
#ASSERT `Do the provisions of our agreement or court order bind the Minister on an assignment` (YearMonthDay 1990 1 1) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Which retirement pensions would an assignment cover` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1960 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1) EQUALS `both retirement pensions`
-- The non-contributor, born 5 May 1960, is 60 from June 2020.
#ASSERT `Which retirement pensions would an assignment cover` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 1960 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1) EQUALS `only the contributor's retirement pension`
#ASSERT `May the Minister approve the assignment of part of my retirement pension` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Minister tell my spouse or partner that I have applied for an assignment` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- April 1968 to May 2012.
#ASSERT `How many months are in our joint contributory period` (YearMonthDay 1950 3 10) (YearMonthDay 1952 7 20) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2012 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2005 12 1) (YearMonthDay 1952 7 20) (YearMonthDay 2013 3 1) FALSE 10 EQUALS 530
-- January 2019 to June 2024.
#ASSERT `How many months are in our first additional joint contributory period` (YearMonthDay 1980 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1985 6 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 6 1) (YearMonthDay 1985 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2024 7 1) EQUALS 66
-- January 2024 to June 2024.
#ASSERT `How many months are in our second additional joint contributory period` (YearMonthDay 1980 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1985 6 15) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 6 1) (YearMonthDay 1985 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2024 7 1) EQUALS 6
-- August 1990 to May 2012.
#ASSERT `How many months are in our period of cohabitation` (YearMonthDay 1990 8 20) (YearMonthDay 2012 5 15) (YearMonthDay 1968 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2012 5 1) EQUALS 262
#ASSERT `What portion of the contributor's retirement pension is assigned to the spouse or partner` 600 100 40 5 530 66 6 EQUALS JUST ((600 TIMES 0.5 TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 530) PLUS (100 TIMES 0.5 TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 66) PLUS (40 TIMES 0.5 TIMES 5 DIVIDED BY 6))
#ASSERT `In which month does the assignment commence` (YearMonthDay 2020 5 17) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1)
-- The earliest of March 2025, November 2024, September 2024, June 2024 and April 2024.
#ASSERT `In which month does the assignment cease` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 11 5) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 9 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 6 20) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2024 3 30) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1)
-- No event has happened yet.
#ASSERT `In which month does the assignment cease` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2023 11 5) FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 9 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 6 20) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 3 30) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May either of us ask in writing for the cancelled assignment to be reinstated` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `On what day is the assignment reinstated` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 20) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2024 5 1)
#ASSERT `Must we both be notified when the Minister approves the assignment` TRUE EQUALS TRUE

§§ `Overpayments, recovery and official error (section 66)`

#ASSERT `How much of a benefit payment must I return at once` 1000 600 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `Is the overpaid amount a debt I owe to the Crown that can be recovered at any time` 1000 600 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the interest I owe under this Part a debt to the Crown` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is a penalty imposed on me under section 90.1 a debt to the Crown` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `How much may be deducted from other amounts payable to me to recover what I owe` 500 800 300 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `On what day may the Minister first certify what I owe` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2021 3 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2021 5 5)
-- Thirty days after a default on 1 March 2021 expire; the next day is 1 April 2021 (31 days).
#ASSERT `On what day may the Minister first certify what I owe` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2021 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2021 3 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1)
#ASSERT `Does the registered certificate have the force of a Federal Court judgment against me` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `May the certificate also be registered in the superior court of my province` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the reasonable costs of registering the certificate be recovered from me` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the certificate be recorded as a charge on my land` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be required to pay money I owe to a debtor of the Crown to the Receiver General` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is an amount I did not pay as the Minister's notice required a debt I owe to the Crown` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is an affidavit of service proof that the Minister's notice was served on me` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `May the Minister remit what I owe` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Convicted in connection with obtaining the payment.
#ASSERT `May the Minister remit what I owe` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the Minister put me back in the position I would be in if official error denied me a benefit, division or assignment` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Minister put right a division I was denied under an agreement or order made before 4 June 1986` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act apply to what I owe under this Part` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act apply to what I owe under this Part` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Cancelling a benefit (section 66.1)`

-- Request on the day 12 months after payment began.
#ASSERT `May I ask to cancel my benefit` `a retirement pension` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 1 15) TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- One day later.
#ASSERT `May I ask to cancel my benefit` `a retirement pension` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 1 16) TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Subsection (1.1): applied for a disability benefit while receiving a retirement pension, deemed disabled after the month it first became payable.
#ASSERT `May I ask to cancel my benefit` `a retirement pension` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2021 6 1) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Repaid by the end of the 12th month after the month it was granted.
#ASSERT `Is my cancelled benefit treated as never having been payable` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2021 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2022 6 30) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my cancelled benefit treated as never having been payable` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2021 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2022 7 1) FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Where the Act, as read here, gives no answer`

-- Died in 1985 with no retirement pension payable: subsection (2)(b) divides the total pensionable earnings by the months in the contributory period, and there are none, so there is no average and no lump sum under (1)(a).
#ASSERT `How much death benefit is paid to the estate of the contributor who died` (YearMonthDay 1985 5 10) FALSE 0 FALSE 120 0 0 100 100 40000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Pension Index for the year of death is nothing to divide by, so the ratio of subsection (3) has no value.
#ASSERT `What base portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month` 300 (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2012 7 20)) 110 2010 2012 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- No Pension Index for the year the contributor died: no ratio.
#ASSERT `What first additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month` TRUE 1000 120 100 (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2012 7 20)) 110 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What second additional portion of the contributor's retirement pension is used for my survivor's pension this month` TRUE 1000 120 100 (YearMonthDay 2012 8 1) (LIST (YearMonthDay 2012 7 20)) 110 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Born 20 June 1975, 45 from 1 July 2020, and the contributor died on 15 June 2010: 121 months under 45, which takes away more than the whole amount, and the text gives no floor.
#ASSERT `How much is my monthly survivor's pension where I get no retirement pension` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1975 6 20) FALSE 100 400 100 200 FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2010 6 15) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2010 6 15) EQUALS NOTHING
-- H is the aggregate of the earnings in subparagraphs 53(1)(b)(i) and (ii); with none, F = G/H has no value, and A is not zero.
#ASSERT `What is the base portion of my monthly post-retirement benefit` (YearMonthDay 1950 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) 0.9 1.42 FALSE 12000 40000 12 9000 0 40000 50000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the first additional portion of my monthly post-retirement benefit` (YearMonthDay 1960 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) 2024 0.9 1.42 FALSE 12000 40000 12 9000 0 40000 50000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the second additional portion of my monthly post-retirement benefit` (YearMonthDay 1960 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) 0.9 1.42 FALSE 12000 20000 12 9000 0 40000 50000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a beneficiary of a retirement pension on 1 January 2021: the subsection deems no application.
#ASSERT `On what day is my application for a post-retirement benefit treated as made` 2020 FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No waiver, no deemed application.
#ASSERT `On what day is my application for a retirement pension treated as made if the Minister waives it` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Neither paragraph (a) nor paragraph (b) applies.
#ASSERT `On what day is an application made after a death treated as received` FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2015 6 15) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Minister is not satisfied: no power to deem.
#ASSERT `In which month can the Minister treat an application made for me as made because I was incapable` (YearMonthDay 2005 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2010 5 20) (YearMonthDay 2009 11 3) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Minister is not satisfied.
#ASSERT `In which month can the Minister treat my application as made because I was incapable until shortly before I applied` (YearMonthDay 2005 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2012 3 10) 100 (YearMonthDay 2012 6 17) (YearMonthDay 2011 2 14) (YearMonthDay 2010 12 5) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Subsection (2) discontinues a pension that is being paid; none is being paid.
#ASSERT `From which month is my survivor's pension discontinued because I remarried` FALSE (YearMonthDay 1985 5 17) (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- No survivor's pension would be payable.
#ASSERT `Which one survivor's pension am I paid if more than one would be payable` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- What is being seized is not a benefit: the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `Is my benefit exempt from seizure and execution` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No authority paid an advance or welfare payment for the period.
#ASSERT `How much may the Minister deduct from my benefit to repay a provincial or municipal authority` FALSE TRUE TRUE 400 1000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Subsection (3) speaks of agreements and orders made on or after 4 June 1986; for an earlier one it says nothing.
#ASSERT `Do the provisions of our agreement or court order bind the Minister on an assignment` (YearMonthDay 1985 12 31) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No months in the joint contributory period: the ratio has no value.
#ASSERT `What portion of the contributor's retirement pension is assigned to the spouse or partner` 600 100 40 5 0 66 6 EQUALS NOTHING
